  "worked_solution": "The vertex is the \"turning point\" of the parabola. In an upwards parabola, like the one here, the vertex is the maximum point. So, the vertex of this parabola is $(5,6).$\n\nThe axis of symmetry is the vertical line that passes through the vertex. Therefore, the axis of symmetry of this parabola is $x=5.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14217628/assets/ed00e2896127e6f3da7fc8e63c22e1944434060ac53e4e63d31f1cd7590a8627.png)",
